From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:58:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: name the degrees-to-turns factor

1/360 turns up as 0.0027777778f, (float)0.0027777778 and
0.002777777845039964 wherever an angle is wrapped. com_math.h now names
it TURNS_PER_DEGREE, as a float (_F) and a double so every use keeps the
type it multiplied by, with static_asserts that each equals the literals
it replaces.

No value changes: the double TURNS_PER_DEGREE stays
0.002777777845039964, the number the code multiplied by, which is not
1.0 / 360.0. cg_pose.cpp multiplies once by the double 0.0027777778, a
different value, and keeps it. First half of upstream issue 45.
